<title>USA: Frontier Corp Q3 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Frontier Corp Q3 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			   3 Months Ended September 30,</p>
<p>				  1996	 1995</p>
<p> Revenues		   $669,069   $571,386</p>
<p>Consolidated Net Income</p>
<p>  (Loss)			73,777  (137,912)</p>
<p>Average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		164,273    152,972</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per</p>
<p>  Common Share		   .45	(.90)</p>
<p>			   9 Months Ended September 30,</p>
<p>				   1996	1995</p>
<p> Revenues		  $1,994,497 $1,537,346</p>
<p> Operating Income	   363,771    175,914</p>
<p>Consolidated Net Income</p>
<p>  (Loss)			200,106   (33,193)</p>
<p>Average common shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		 163,960    150,742</p>
<p>Earnings (Loss) Per</p>
<p>  Common Share		   1.22	(.23)</p>
<p>NOTE - Q3 1995 includes one-time, after-tax charges of $195.1 million related to acquisitions and extraordinary items.</p>
<p>First nine months results ending September 30, 1996, include an after-tax charge in the 1996 Q1 of $6.9 million, or $0.04 per share, related to a mandatory change in accounting principle, union contract negotiations at its Rochester, N.Y., operation, and a gain on a sale. Results for the same period in 1995 include a gain on a sale and several one-time charges.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk, 212 859-1610</p>
